  "body": "You have the option to purchase property 3A, property 3B, or both. Offered to the market for the very first time, these stunning masonry render and mixed materials homes present a rare chance to secure a unique coastal holding in one of Auckland's most prestigious suburbs. Cherished by the same family for over 30 years, both residences are now ready for their next chapter. \r\n\r\nSet on a combined 506m2 freehold site, the properties offer exceptional flexibility, whether you are searching for your forever home, a multi-generational living solution, or a smart investment with the option to purchase one or both together. The site is zoned Residential - Terrace Housing and Apartment Buildings, providing future development potential in this blue-chip location.\r\n\r\n3A - Elevated Coastal Living\r\nWake each morning to breathtaking sea views, enjoying a lifestyle defined by light, space, and coastal serenity. This beautifully presented home features:\r\n\r\n* 3 spacious bedrooms, including two master ensuites\r\n* A well-appointed family bathroom\r\n* A generous open-plan living zone with a large kitchen\r\n* Expansive living and dining areas designed for effortless everyday comfort\r\n\r\n3B - Modern Living With Work-From-Home Flexibility\r\nDesigned for contemporary lifestyles, 3B offers:\r\n\r\n* 3 bedrooms, 2 bathrooms, plus a dedicated home office\r\n* A large open-plan living area flowing seamlessly to outdoor entertaining spaces\r\n* A layout ideal for families, professionals, or those seeking additional flexibility\r\n\r\nShared Features\r\nBoth homes include:\r\n\r\n* Internal access double garages\r\n* Huge storage areas or workshop spaces (3B)\r\n\r\nUnbeatable St Heliers Location\r\nJust moments from the beach, cafes, restaurants, parks, and the vibrant St Heliers village. Families will appreciate zoning for St Heliers Bay School and Glendowie College, two of Auckland's most sought-after schools. Coastal walkways, sports clubs, and public transport are all within easy reach.\r\n\r\nProperties of this calibre are tightly held and seldom available. After three decades of family memories, the current owners now pass this special coastal holding to its next custodian.",
